# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cochange_rename.py" "COCHANGE RENAME-FOLLOW GATE: PASS" "co-change rename-follow (a renamed file's split history is recovered as ONE continuous history)" "co-change rename-follow: 'git log --name-only' reports a file's OLD path before a rename and its NEW path after, so the SAME logical file looks like TWO short, unrelated files -> its co-change history is SPLIT in half and each half can fall BELOW the support floor -> a real coupling SILENTLY VANISHES (the fleet measured 9-59% of co-change recall is recoverable just by following renames). The fix lives in the HISTORY/BACKFILL path only (_cg_cochange._git_log_commits, reached only via the blobless clone -> populate_cochange*; NOT the live per-push path): it reads '--name-status -M' (a status letter + paths + a rename arrow 'R<sim> old new' -- still NO diff / message / author / body) and CANONICALISES every historical path to the file's CURRENT name, so the pair is computed on the UNIFIED history. Recall is RECOVERED, never INVENTED -- it only MERGES two path-histories of the SAME file (a COPY 'C old new' is NOT a rename and does not unify). Proven on a crafted temp repo: a file co-changes with a partner, is git-mv'd, keeps co-changing under the new name -- WITHOUT follow the (renamed,partner) pair's support is SPLIT below 6; WITH follow the unified history yields the coupled pair at full support 6. The precision discipline is intact: the GIANT commit is still skipped, the once-seen coincidence is still dropped, lift still divides out the base rate; content-free (paths + counts only)" "co-change rename-follow recovers a renamed file's split history as ONE continuous history (--name-status -M canonicalised to the current path) in the backfill path only -- support unified, lift/support/giant-skip discipline preserved, content-free" 26
